From: Tyler Baker <tyler@foundries.io>
Date: Tue, 27 May 2026
Subject: firmware: qcom: scm: allow qseecom on arduino,imola (UNO Q)

The qcom_scm qseecom interface guards against unvalidated machines via
qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[]: of_machine_device_match() against the DT
root "compatible" walk, falling back to "untested machine, skipping" if
no entry matches. The Arduino UNO Q (QRB2210 / qcom,qcm2290) is one of
those skipped machines today, which leaves Linux without a working
proxy to the TZ-side TAs (uefisecapp et al), and in turn leaves UEFI
runtime variable services returning EFI_DEVICE_ERROR (status=0x80000000_00000007)
from get_next_variable():

  $ dmesg | grep efivars
  [2.941219] efivars: get_next_variable: status=8000000000000007

  $ ls /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/ | wc -l
  0

  $ findmnt /boot
  (nothing — systemd-gpt-auto-generator gives up because
   LoaderDevicePartUUID is never set in efivars)

UNO Q's DT root compatible is:
  arduino,imola
  qcom,qrb2210
  qcom,qcm2290

This matches the existing allowlist pattern (board-level identifiers
like "qcom,glymur-crd", "asus,vivobook-s15") so add "arduino,imola".

After this patch:
  - qcom_scm: convention: smc arm 64
  - qcom_scm firmware:scm: qseecom: found qseecom with version 0x1402000
  - (no "untested machine, skipping")
  - qseecom platform device registered
  - userspace can issue TA invocations via qseecom

Note: this alone does not guarantee UEFI runtime variables come up
on the QRB2210 (the EDK2 runtime variable path may still fail at the
uefisecapp <-> uefivarstore layer). But it is the prerequisite the
kernel-side check has been blocking.

Risk: the comment immediately above the allowlist states "We do not
yet support re-entrant calls via the qseecom interface. To prevent
any potential issues with this, only allow validated machines for
now." We have not verified that the QRB2210 platform avoids the
re-entrant qseecom pattern; if it doesn't, qseecom calls could
deadlock. The fallback (no qseecom binding) is the current state.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local enablement / awaiting validation]
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler@foundries.io>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2287,6 +2287,7 @@
  + any potential issues with this, only allow validated machines for now.
  */
 static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
+	{ .compatible = "arduino,imola" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15-x1p4" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407qa" },
